! GAME=../entharion/zcode-inform/custard-r1-s000314.z7
! SEED=57452

# Custard reads its whole command line through its own read_char
# editor -- the machinery behind its xyzzy input-mangling gimmick
# -- so every command needs an explicit > enter after it, the
# Bureaucracy convention. The name is a true line read and the
# gender pick is a single keystroke; neither takes an enter.

Jeff
m

i
>
examine uniform
>
examine tag
>
examine broom
>
examine pie
>
examine clockwork
>
take pie
>
eat pie
>
examine table
>
examine moon
>
n
>
examine breaker
>
turn on breaker
>
# The breaker starts the game's famous effect: the digits of pi
# roll up every blank space on the screen. It is pure animation
# -- the game expects you to keep playing straight through it.
eat pie
>
examine gear
>
u
>
# The choice the game poses: lose your broom or your legs. The
# broom wedged in the gear keeps the legs -- and the legs are what
# turn off the lights at the end.
put broom in gear
>
examine me
>
i
>
examine dollar
>
examine man
>
ask man about custard
>
ask man about me
>
# Buying the replacement custard returns you to the Bakery, lights
# on, with the game's own hint: leave it on the table and go home.
buy custard
>
examine pie
>
n
>
turn off lights
>
s
>
# The ending: your boss, custard on his face, "You pie switching
# bastard!"
put pie on table
>
